A||||27||Jimmy||V8 FUN, Engine swap complete!!!!!||||1||
Z||000000||Jimmy||07-15-2001||11:52 PM||||All I can say is  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Thankyou Archie, KEV, and Jaei Sun!  <P>I finaly took the beast out and my god is it fast.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  I am very surprised at how docile the V8 is when your not getting on it.  Feels almost like my 2.8 at idle and also when I'm just cruising around.  I am still breaking in the centerforce clutch and engine(500 miles till broken in) but it certainly pulls at least as good as my brother's 91 5.0 at half the throttle.  <P>After breaking it in I'll try and visit a local dyno(dunno of one) and then after some more tuning I'll visit a track.  My engine builder builds many 350s like mine and he says they run about 275 HP or so at the rear wheels in f-bodies.  I know fieros have less drivetrain loss than f-bodies so I am hoping for close to 300HP.<P>Well its time to get back out to the car and go thru a nut and bolt check.  I'll post more later after a little tuning also.<P>Jim<P>87 GT <BR>87 GT T-TOP V8  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Jaei Sun||07-16-2001||12:43 AM||||Hell yeah!  I'll have to check this beast out.<P>What was the trouble with the clutch?  Bet ya can't wait till it's broken in so you can eat that BMW m3!||||reg||1
Z||000002||Jimmy||07-16-2001||01:03 AM||||Well the problem with the clutch was not a problem that needed to have me pull everything apart again! doh-  I just needed to replace the rod in the slave with a bigger one, go figure.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>I just got done giving my brother a ride and his eyes lit up, the word SCARY came out of his mouth a couple of times.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Now I know how Kaas(sp?)felt after he picked up his car from Archie's and drove it out to the Dells earlier this year.  He was so excited he just had to show it to somebody, luckily that somebody was me!  He also used the word SCARY a few times. <P>Jim<BR>87 GT<BR>87 GT T-TOP V8<p>[This message has been edited by Jimmy (edited 07-16-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||KRMFiero||07-16-2001||06:54 AM||||What Tranny did you use? 4 speed? 5 speed?...<P>Kyle||||reg||1
Z||000004||BRIAN CORNELIUS||07-16-2001||09:23 AM||||JIMMY,<BR>Too bad you did not have it ready for the Saturday nite get together. It was great. Tina and elfiero had their V-8 Fieros there. and Standard had his quad 4 conversion. Jaeisun, Dslice, lowfiero, and a couple other Fiero supporters were there. I am still redoing the front end on my v-8 conversion, but the conversion is basically done.<BR> <BR>There is a great dynos shop in crystal you could use to chcek your HP. S&S PERFORMANCE at 5141 Laneland Av. N.: 612-536-0376.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Archie||07-16-2001||11:00 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Jimmy:<BR><B>All I can say is   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif">   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Jim<P>87 GT <BR>87 GT T-TOP V8   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Congrats man, the fun has just started.<P>Archie||||reg||1
Z||000006||Jimmy||07-16-2001||11:29 AM||||Kyle I used the 5 speed Muncie/Getrag tranny.  I was going to rebuild the tranny(95,000 miles) but a couple local tranny experts recommended to NOT rebuild it unless it is showing signs of wear.  It shifts fine and the rebuild kit I bought from Rodney Dickman($12.50) helps take out the slack of the original gear selector bracket.<P>Jim<P>87 GT<BR>87 GT T-TOP V8||||reg||1
Z||000007||kempo||07-16-2001||12:59 PM||||SO cool!  I want a v8!  About how much $ did you have to put into it for it's completed state?  Also, to anybody with a v8 fiero, could you post your best 0-60 and quarter times?  Thanks!  Best of luck Jimmy!<P>-Kemp||||reg||6
Z||000008||Jimmy||07-16-2001||01:09 PM||||Kempo I spent just under $4K for my V8 swap I spent $2k on the car.  Archie started a whole thread on this and I give more details on what I did, do a search.<P>Quarter mile times, I haven't seen any slips but there are Fiero V8's in MN that get into the mid 12's.  In fact from what I hear there is a guy that ran consistant 12.6, 12.7 all summer and decided to build up his motor some more, should be hearing about his new times soon.<P>Jim||||reg||1
Z||000009||KnightRyder31||07-16-2001||01:22 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Jimmy:<BR><B>Kempo I spent just under $4K for my V8 swap I spent $2k on the car.  Archie started a whole thread on this and I give more details on what I did, do a search.<P>Quarter mile times, I haven't seen any slips but there are Fiero V8's in MN that get into the mid 12's.  In fact from what I hear there is a guy that ran consistant 12.6, 12.7 all summer and decided to build up his motor some more, should be hearing about his new times soon.<P>Jim</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>I think California Kid's did it in 12.2!<BR>||||reg||1
