Z||000011||FieroLT1||07-16-2001||02:17 PM||||Congratulations!!!<BR>Now, go to your closest school supplies store and get a small chalk board and some chalk.<BR>Make columns for 'thangs | 'Vettes |||161.49.21.100||reg||10
Z||000012||mrfixit58||07-16-2001||05:07 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Sootah:<BR><B>What kinda gas mileage do you get w/ a V8 in a Fiero?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>HeHeHe... If you want gas mileage, stick with stock. If you install a TPI 350 AND the 5-speed, you MIGHT be able to squeak out 22MPG highway 16 city. The final gear ratio is still pretty high. The N* with Caddy with OD tranny is quoted at getting 24 hwy. Performance costs $$$. Nothing magical about it.<P><P>------------------<BR>Roy :D<BR>87 GT   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pennocksize.JPG"> ||||reg||10
Z||000013||California Kid||07-16-2001||05:36 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Sootah:<BR><B>What kinda gas mileage do you get w/ a V8 in a Fiero?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Los Angeles to St. Louis in 32 hours netted 21 miles per gallon, and that included 4 hours in snow between Flagstaff and Albuque (had to keep going to keep going because they were going to close X-way for a day or two). Won't disclose speeds, you do the math!!  I seem to get 21 mpg no matter what I do with the car.||||reg||1
