Z||000017||Joe Torma||07-16-2001||07:24 PM||||I have to ask you all with the V8s...is the handling wierd with more weight to the right or is it ok, offset with the battery/other weight relocation?<P>Joe<BR>3400series 300hp||||reg||1
Z||000018||gt2437||07-16-2001||08:09 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Joe Torma:<BR><B>I have to ask you all with the V8s...is the handling wierd with more weight to the right or is it ok, offset with the battery/other weight relocation?<P>Joe<BR>3400series 300hp</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>the engine may be to the right, but the driver sits to the left -just don't take along any passengers  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>||||reg||1
Z||000019||California Kid||07-16-2001||09:26 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Joe Torma:<BR><B>I have to ask you all with the V8s...is the handling wierd with more weight to the right or is it ok, offset with the battery/other weight relocation?<P>Joe<BR>3400series 300hp</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Mine handles like a "slot car", 1.17G in turns, you just have to choose the right suspension parts and frt/rr wheel alignment settings to get you there. An aluminum head small block with 4 Core radiator only adds 100 lbs to the vehicle weight. Battery placement can be either on the left side of engine compartment or in front trunk (mine is on left side of engine compartment).<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000020||Jimmy||07-17-2001||01:33 PM||||Frontal Lobe the entire motor with a professional rebuild cost me $800. I did an engine swap for a friend on his 74 Nova.  He gave me his old motor we took out of the car.  I have a friend that owns a machine shop.  All he does is rebuild Big blocks and small blocks, his wife does 302's and 351's.  I gave him my tired 350($0) and left it with him for 6 months.  He worked on it when he had spare time and I paid for mainly just the parts($800).  <P>The exhaust cost me $113.60 for material and installation.  This was a STEAL.  My exhaust is not as loud as I thought it would be, I am running a set of glasspacks with 2 3/4 pipe.  I had the guy modify my collectors on the stock tips to accept the 2 3/4 pipe so it has the appearance of being stock.  Ask Jaei Sun or KEV about my exahust they will tell you it is pretty good quality and is pretty tame compared to most high performance cars.  Can't remember what the tach read at 80 but at 70mph it was about 2500rpm and at 65 it was 2300rpm.  <P>Joe the car has no real handling differences that I can really feel yet.  Of course I haven't really thrown it around yet like if I were on a track.  I relocated the battery up front using the "Jaei Sun Method" which helps I assume.  During this swap I also upgraded the brakes, poly all around and lowered the front.  I still have stock suspension in back, it sits the same as my V6 in the back.  I still have the big nasty wheel well gap in back.  I am going to buy a swaybar for the rear and coilovers with 350# springs.  It feels better than stock for handling now and I defintely don't feel any quirkieness in the car.  I'll post more later about the handling when I drive it more.<P>Jim||||reg||1
Z||000021||RiceCooker||07-17-2001||02:05 PM||||Congrats and welcome to the V8 fiero club<P>(ssshh, I'm pretending i have a v8  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">)||||reg||6
