Z||000027||Jimmy||07-18-2001||02:30 AM||||I have had a REALLY FUN DAY today.  I put about 100 miles on the car today just driving up and down a 10 mile stretch of freeway.  Just getting a feel for the car and making sure the coolant system works.  Right now I am running without a thermostat.  I tried a 180 but it didn't seem to work so well, tomorow I am going to try a 160.  I am now running my fan all the time.  BTW todays weather in Minneapolis was about 100 degrees with 80 for humidity, good day to test the cooling system.  <P>I will drive my other fiero in the winter.  <P>Archie, you can borrow the car for the winter and keep the T-TOPs if it comes back in the spring with that convertable top you bought!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><BR>Standard, I most certainly will bring the car to the next meet.  Seems like we will have more fieros with different motors in them at the meet then stock ones.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Jaei Sun show up tomorow night if you can.<P>Tomorow I'll throw the car around to see how it handles.<P>Jim<P>87 GT<BR>87 GT T-TOP V8<P>BTW I walked all over a new GTP tonight on the freeway.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I was more surprised then the GTP driver, this was really the first time I really got on it. Damn fast, pulls like hell in fifth gear, too bad I have to shut it down around 4grand cause the motor and clutch are brand new.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">||||reg||1
